 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Points to consider when choosing small equipment:\n• its use and the needs of the family;\n• the material: strong, safe, does not rust, easy to clean;\n• good quality and finish (no sharp edges, tight lids, firm handles that do not conduct heat);\n• size and weight; price and money available; storage space.\nCare:\n• wash in hot soapy water soon after use, rinse and dry well;\n• soak pots with burnt food before scrubbing; do not scrub non-stick pans with steel wool;\n• keep knives sharp and store them safely in a block or rack, never loose in water;\n• dry wooden tools quickly (they crack and grow mould if soaked);\n• store tools in clean, dry places; oil cast iron to stop rust.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "t": "a wooden spoon"
  },
  "problem": "How should {t} be cared for?",
  "steps": [
   "Wash it quickly in hot soapy water; do not leave it soaking.",
   "Dry it well and store it in a dry place, so it does not crack or grow mould."
  ],
  "answer": "Wash quickly, dry well and store dry; never soak it.",
  "checks": []
 },
